choice("Continue", B2-Ch11b-Fatigue, v_current_scene = B2-Ch11b-Fatigue)


ID: B2-Ch11b-Uneasy
TEXT:

 "Actually, you look pretty shaken yourself. Did something happen during your ritual?"

"The only problem with my ritual was that there weren't enough battles," Hadrik says. "I was expecting a real fight, you know? It was a letdown."

"Oh, you were expecting a real fight, dwarf?" Arraka says. "That's funny, because that's not how it looked from what I saw."

"What do you know about my ritual?..." Hadrik says, the tension instantly returning to his eyes.

"More than you think, dwarf," Arraka says. "And I'm not talking only about your trial from the God of Time. I glanced through your memories too while you were locked in stasis. I saw some very interesting things connected to that trial. Want me to share them with the group?"

